A1. What is a wise cracker sometimes called? ~ CARD
A4. Where do monks live? ~ ABBEY
A8. What part of speech represents action? ~ VERB
A11. What was the first name of a famous Highland freebooter? ~ ROB
A13. What do flighty young men get? ~ AIR
A14. What would the Kaiser have gotten if he had found his place in the sun? ~ TAN
A15. Name a preposition. ~ AT
A17. What could you call a shy young man who would never get wise? ~ EVERGREEN
A18. If money makes the mare go, what makes her stop? ~ HO
A19. What is a kittenish thing to do? ~ MEW
A21. What is just a little one? ~ TOT
A22. What must you have to appreciate music? ~ EAR
A23. What birds are similar to gulls? (Plural.) ~ TERNS
A25. Name a kind of rat trap. ~ CAT
A28. How do political opponents look to conservative politicians? ~ RED
A31. What often makes a hit with the school teacher? ~ PELLET
A34. What has every stubborn jackass done in his day? ~ BALKED
A36. What do critics love to do? ~ RAP
A37. What kind of person prefers the primrose path? ~ REVELER
A38. Name an adverb that refers to the past. ~ AGO
A39. What kind of type is often used for emphasis? ~ ITALIC
A40. Who is not generally accredited with "taking ways"? ~ EDITOR
A41. What did the boys do in the past generation for a kiss? ~ ASK
A43. What drink does Judge, Jr. never talk about? ~ TEA
A44. What is Alexander called in the history books? ~ GREAT
A45. Who raised Cain a long time ago? ~ EVE
A47. What kind of tree is horizontal 17? ~ FIR
A50. What is noted for its prominent tooth? ~ ELK
A52. Where should the Prince of Wales stay? ~ ON
A53. What is three-in-one? ~ THREEFOLD
A56. Name a personal pronoun. ~ ME
A57. Name something sheepish. ~ EWE
A58. Name a kind of slipper worn in Canada. ~ SKI
A59. What has the U. S. A. been since prohibition was passed? (This is a joke.) ~ DRY
A61. What has the last word? ~ ECHO
A62. What is the end of anything? ~ STERN
A63. What should salesmen do to succeed? ~ SELL

D1. What would officials have to do to fill the jails if prohibition were enforced? ~ CRAM
D2. What runs and leaves tracks behind? (abbr.) ~ RR
D3. What is a deer thing? ~ DOE
D5. Who is a regular cut up? ~ BARBER
D6. What was Samson? ~ BIG
D7. What message does the messenger boy rarely ever run? ~ ERRAND
D8. What usually gets loaded about October 1st? ~ VAN
D9. What is half the square of a type? ~ EN
D10. What goes around a foot? ~ BOOT
D12. What is often next to the men? ~ BVD
D14. What are 4 Chinese, 4 Indians and 2 Englishmen? ~ TEN
D16. What do some folks use for a drive? ~ TEE
D18. What kind of dogs have no ears? ~ HOT
D20. What used to hang around the house when father was a boy? ~ WALLPAPER
D21. What are women politicians? ~ TALKATIVE
D24. What is divorce? ~ RELEASE
D26. Name a month of the year. ~ APRIL
D27. What brought honors to Lindbergh? ~ MERIT
D29. What is the last kid to get to school? ~ TARDY
D30. What does your nose know? (Plural.) ~ ODORS
D32. What is a silly thing to do in a night club? ~ EAT
D33. What does a thief call a detective? ~ TEC
D34. What follows the queen wherever she goes? ~ BEE
D35. What is noticeable about all actors? ~ EGO
D41. What do criminals dodge in Chicago? ~ ARREST
D42. What is a South African Bantu? ~ KAFFIR
D43. What can be found in a Ford any Sunday afternoon? ~ TIN
D46. What well-known tree is found in Europe and America? ~ ELM
D47. What is the call of the wild golfer? ~ FORE
D48. Name a book by H. Rider Haggard. ~ SHE
D49. What is an African Bantu at the age of seventy? ~ OLD
D51. What supports the frame of a boat? ~ KEEL
D53. What does it take to get married? ~ TWO
D54. What verb means "to supply what is wanted"? ~ EKE
D55. Who bury their mistakes? (abbr.) ~ DRS
D57. Name an exclamation. ~ EH
D60. What was a definite article in Old England? ~ YE


